# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4-serve-5 window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/serve-4 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN.
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. Every value is final.
# ORDER.txt says the order, each job's image, its stop rule and its minutes. The image is tp4-serve-5 throughout: B5 builds it, the
# later jobs serve it, and a commit after B5's tag needs a new tag and every later job the new one.
# FX5e: the fix arm of the audits-off hang on tp4-serve-5, c2-packed-tp4-speed-fix (gate only): audits OFF, tail caps ON, the capture
# plug (QWEN_FAST_CAPTURE_PLUG=1, engines too; per bank leave 512, reserve 256, engine 256, floor 128 MB), the stall watch (120 s, its
# triage now able to run: ttexalens is in the image) and the collective handle guard in log mode. v186 failed at attach ('Out of Memory'
# in 'stage capture plug seal': the seal plugged the whole reserve); the seal now never plugs the reserve hole and refuses with a clear
# error under the floor. The test list is the hang shapes only: warmup, coding, long_real_text, concurrent4
# (the v164 four-user sequential tail), concurrent4_v164order, concurrent4_steady (the v172 steady engine build after 200+ packed rounds), replay_concurrent4
# (the platform replay's request shape) and concurrent4_code.
# FX5a..FX5e are FIVE IDENTICAL jobs: the acceptance bar is five consecutive passes on this one image, each after its own card reset
# (the actions say reset smoke). One failure restarts the count: stop, keep the log, and run D5 (the diagnosis repro with working triage).
# READ the log: (1) the attach: '[PINDIAG] capture plug packed' open, sealed and released once with no error and no out-of-memory, then one
# open and one sealed per engine build; the monitor lines with free_mb never under the floor. (2) no hang: every test returns, no '[STALL]'
# line, no replay-deadline exit, every concurrent4 and concurrent4_steady user at 800 tokens, every replay_concurrent4 user at 300.
# (3) any '[STALL]' brings '[TRIAGE-CHECK] ready' and the tools' output: keep it. (4) hashes equal B5's for the same test.
# Duration (estimate): 25 min per run. Not a stop job.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-5
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-speed-fix
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,long_real_text,concurrent4,concurrent4_v164order,concurrent4_steady,replay_concurrent4,concurrent4_code
